  "final": "Done.\n\n- **Verified in Chrome** (Playwright against this repo's `serve.py`, at 375px and 1280px):\n  - **Row Delete button:** it opens the confirmation dialog.\n  - **Escape:** it cancels and keeps all 5 rows.\n  - **Confirm:** it removes the row (5 → 4) and shows the toast `Deleted “Website redesign”`.\n  - **Layout:** there is no horizontal overflow at either width, and the long project names wrap cleanly beside the button.\n  - **Tests:** `python3 -m unittest` passes (4 tests).\n- **Console 404:** a 404 appeared once, on the phone run only. I didn't trace it. It is probably the favicon request.\n- **Port 8765:** another server was already running on it, so my first browser run hit that server's files instead of this repo's. I discarded those results and re-ran against my own server on port 8791.\n- **Persistence:** deletes live in memory only, so a reload brings the rows back. `data.js` is static and the task didn't ask for persistence.\n\nThe changes are in `app.js` and `styles.css`.",
